 "notes": "Wreck plan of the Giannis D (99.5 x 16 m) at the western corner of Abu Nuhas: stern section canted about 45 degrees to port with the engine room, bridge and funnel, a flattened midships and the bow on its port side, lying roughly parallel to the reef with the stern to the west. Position and reef edge from OpenStreetMap; dimensions, layout and depths from the Red Sea Wreck Project and dive-guide descriptions (stern 24-26 m, mast top 4 m, bow about 10 m); the route is the usual east-bound swim with the reef on the right. The RIB drop, feature positions along the hull and intermediate depths are approximate.",
